/target/
.superpowers/

# The durable engineering record under .claude/ IS tracked: the spec of
# record, the phase plans, the measurement evidence, the QA scripts and the
# conventions are the reasoning behind every budget and hard rule in this
# repo, and a reviewer who cannot read them cannot check the code against
# its own contract. What stays untracked below is either machine-local
# (scratch, temp, per-user settings) or an operational log rather than a
# durable record.
.claude/tmp/
.claude/scratch/
.claude/bench-baselines/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/.headroom_wrap_marker.json
# Per-user hook wiring (auto-executing hooks are a supply-chain exposure in a
# public repo, and the wiring bakes machine-local paths) and the maintainer's
# session-operational logs. The hook scripts under .claude/hooks/ stay tracked.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/HANDOFF.md
.claude/STATUS.md
.claude/known-bugs.md
.claude/archive/
.claude/pending-first-push.md
/compat/.cache/
/compat/results.json

# a diagnostic a failed matrix run leaves for hand-diffing against the
# baseline; committing one would put unratcheted numbers in the repo
*.partial.toml

# every gate run's own measured cells, uploaded as a CI artifact for
# seating a cell or re-sizing a headroom entry; same reason as above,
# these are raw draws and never a recorded bar
*.measured.toml

# a replicate campaign's proposal: the seats, factors and draws N gated
# replicates resolve to, for review. Same reason again -- what a campaign
# writes is a proposal nothing reads, and what gets committed is the
# reviewed content of it inside the real baseline and its sidecar
*.campaign.toml

# cpython's own bytecode cache. Running scripts/test-fixtures/delay-relay
# (this tree's only Python fixture; its siblings are /bin/sh) directly as
# __main__ writes none, so this is a safety net for anyone who later
# imports it as a module or byte-compiles it by hand (`python3 -m
# py_compile`), not a cache this tree's own test runs generate.
__pycache__/
